WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.377
"Ginkgo and Nicotinamide for Glaucoma Treatment"

00:00:07.445 --> 00:00:10.140
Glaucoma is now
the leading cause

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.960
of irreversible vision loss
in the world.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.260
It's caused by the deterioration
of the optic nerve

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.000
that connects the eye
to the brain.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.940
Most commonly this is due
to excessive pressure

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.140
inside the eyeball.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.160
Ginkgo biloba is one
of the most common supplements

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.900
taken by glaucoma sufferers.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.840
It doesn't seem to lower
intraocular pressure,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.900
but MRI studies suggest
ginkgo supplements may increase

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.760
cerebral blood flow
in the brain.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.700
What about blood flow
to the eyes?

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.460
Ginkgo increases
ocular blood flow

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:43.740
in both normal
and glaucomatous subjects;

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.080
so, it was put to the test.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.400
Compared to sugar pills,

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.160
40 milligrams
of a ginkgo extract twice a day,

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.440
on top of their regular
anti-glaucoma medications,

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.560
appeared to significantly slow
the progression

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.160
of visual defects
in open-angle glaucoma patients,

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.000
the most common type,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.040
though it's not clear
in this study

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.500
if the participants
were properly randomized.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.800
Aside from
a single published case report

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.440
of visual improvements
after ginkgo supplementation,

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.200
there don't appear
to be any other studies

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.760
on open-angle glaucoma,

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.560
but there have been
two interventional trials

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.020
on the less common
normal tension type.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.780
They were both randomized,
double-blind,

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.520
placebo-controlled
crossover trials

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:24.900
using the same dose
and duration.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.240
One found
a significant benefit,

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.940
an improvement in pre-existing
visual field damage,

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.400
but the other found
no benefit at all.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.700
If you want to try it despite
the underwhelming results,

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.940
make sure to first discuss with
your healthcare professional

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:42.600
due to a possible increase
in bleeding risk from the herb.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.780
Any other supplement
possibilities?

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:47.100
In 2017,

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.800
extraordinary results
were reported

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.120
in a leading scientific journal.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.180
Nicotinamide,
a form of vitamin B3,

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.820
was able to prevent
the development of glaucoma

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.800
in aged mice
prone to the disease,

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.740
with more than 90 percent
effectiveness.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.900
Moderate or severe nerve damage

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.820
was found in about two-thirds
of the control mice,

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:09.600
but 93 percent of the mice
given nicotinamide had none.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.460
The researchers concluded,

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:15.120
"The degree of protection
afforded by administering

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.100
this single molecule
is unprecedented

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.920
and unanticipated."

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.240
A commentary on the study

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.580
published in the New England
Journal of Medicine entitled,

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:26.040
"Nicking Glaucoma
with Nicotinamide?"

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.040
suggested clinical trials
should be initiated.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.280
The researchers thought
to give it a try

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.560
based on the fact
that glaucomatous mice

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.920
had a comparable deficiency
in NAD+,

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.740
from which nicotinamide
is a precursor.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.320
Is that even the case in people?

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.460
Apparently so.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:45.660
Those with glaucoma

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.880
have about a third lower
nicotinamide levels

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.160
in their blood
compared to age-matched peers.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.640
And greater intake of niacin,
which is another form of B3,

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.680
is associated
with less glaucoma.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.860
It was time
to put it to the test,

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.260
and the title gives it away.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.520
In 2020,

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.560
an international team
of researchers

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.540
published a study
in which glaucoma patients

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.580
were randomized
to nicotinamide or placebo

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.640
for 12 weeks and then switched
for another 12 weeks.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.860
And significantly fewer patients

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.020
suffered further
visual field deterioration

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.520
while on the nicotinamide,

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.920
4 percent versus 12 percent
while on placebo.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.420
A 2022 study found significant
improvements in visual function

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.340
compared to placebo
within two months,

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.260
but it's not
directly comparable,

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.880
since they also added pyruvate,

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.920
which is another component
of energy metabolism.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:35.700
For a discussion of cost,
labeling confusion,

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.640
and potential side effects
of taking nicotinamide,

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.480
check out the NAD chapter
in my book How Not to Age,

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.760
in which I go through
the pros and cons

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:48.060
of all nine
NAD-boosting supplements,

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.700
it's like a tongue twister:

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:57.890
NA, NAM, NMN, NR,
NAD, NADH, NMNH, NRH,

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.730
tryptophan.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.600
Or you just stay tuned here
on NutritionFacts.org

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.880
for an upcoming series
of videos on the subject.

